      <h2 id='data'>Data</h2>
      <p>Postgres runs under CloudNativePG as a highly available cluster, with one instance required per node, on the TrueNAS iSCSI storage described in <a href='/server.html#today'>what the homelab runs on today</a>. Each service that holds data gets its own database and role on that cluster, and grants keep them apart.</p>
      <p>In Aug 2026 the backup story grew up:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>barman point-in-time recovery replaced the nightly <code>pg_dump</code>, so a restore can land on a chosen moment rather than last night</li>
        <li>the workload-identity tokens that authorize those backups are now published whenever they rotate, instead of on a fixed timer</li>
        <li>WAL retention for replication slots is capped, so a stalled slot cannot hold on to WAL indefinitely</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id='observability'>Observability <small>May 2026</small></h2>
      <p>The services are instrumented with OpenTelemetry, and ingest exports its own pipeline metrics to a Grafana dashboard, so an import can be followed from upload onward.</p>

